<Base title="Sources and policy" description="How IntoTheTwilightZone.com sources its facts and handles copyrighted material.">
  <h1>Sources and policy</h1>
  <p class="lead">This site hosts facts, original writing and short attributed excerpts. Everything else is linked, not copied.</p>
  <h2>What the site publishes</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Facts: titles, air dates, credits, runtimes and production codes, organised in our own structure.</li>
    <li>Original writing: synopses, essays, lists and analysis written for this site.</li>
    <li>Short excerpts with citations: a sentence or two of narration, the single lyric line that mentions the show, or a brief public quote about its influence.</li>
    <li>Public-domain and freely licensed material, with attribution.</li>
  </ul>
  <h2>What the site links to instead</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Episodes, clips, trailers and music: official channels and streaming services.</li>
    <li>Scripts, letters, academic essays, manuals and magazine scans: the archive, library or publisher that holds them.</li>
  </ul>
  <h2>How connections are graded</h2>
  <dl class="facts">
    <dt><span class="tag confirmed-by-creator">Confirmed by the creator</span></dt><dd>The later work's creator has said so publicly, with a cited source.</dd>
    <dt><span class="tag documented">Documented</span></dt><dd>A reliable published source makes the connection.</dd>
    <dt><span class="tag fan-noted">Fan-noted</span></dt><dd>A widely noticed resemblance with no source yet. Shown for completeness and clearly labelled.</dd>
  </dl>
  <h2>Corrections and takedown</h2>
  <p>See <a href="/about/#contact">Contact and corrections</a>.</p>
</Base>
